A||||13||onfire||Fast and the Furious Fiero.||||1||
Z||000000||onfire||07-18-2001||03:46 AM||||Someone wanted to know if a Fiero would fit under a container, in another post along time ago. Well the answer is yes and, no. Yes it will fit if the container is not moving, and the landing gear is lowered all the way (thus raising the front of it as high as it will go, with about 2 inches to spare). No it will not fit if the container is moving, even if we used the Ottowa to pick up the container, and drive around. The frame of the container is to low. Even if the Fiero was lowered and the top was chopped, it still wouldn't fit. See photos below. We used a 53 foot over the road container. It had the most ground clearance of all the containers we had in the yard at the time. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/willbycar.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/willincar.jpg"> <P><FONT COLOR="#ff0000">Disclaimer:</FONT><BR>Don't try this at home or on the road. And aahhhh don't show my boss these pics. Thanks in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||onfire||07-18-2001||03:47 AM||||P.S. That is my friend Willi and his Fiero.||||reg||1
